From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rbb-dev <37469229+rbb-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:04:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: the server's context window is what a stream holds, so
 a request with no max_tokens is served

The lanes place a stream only when prompt + max_new + round_rows + 2, in whole 2,048-row chunks, fits ctx_cap
(lanes.zig prefillFn). The server was told the whole window and clamped a request that sent no max_tokens to
exactly window - prompt, which the lanes then refused (PromptTooLong, HTTP 500): every request without max_tokens
failed (2026-10-27: a 1,577-token tool call, 9 times). rows.zig holds both rules; native.zig reports
usableRows(ctx_cap, round_rows, chunk) and native/cuda.zig gives it to the server as its context window when the
family reports one (other families unchanged). A request with no max_tokens now gets every token left; one that
asks for more than fits is refused by the server (HTTP 400, with the most it may ask).

Tests: rows.zig: the server's room fits the lanes exactly at every prompt size and one token more does not, for
several windows and round sizes; 1,048,576 tokens with 48-row rounds = 1,048,526. The dsv41 suite (LLVM, x86_64):
120 pass, 1 fails, the same 1 as without this commit (draft chances, 0.547 vs 0.5).
